    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2578",
      "problem": "In the figure below, $m \\angle BAE = {110}^{\\circ}.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/245dbaa430eb99aee193110fcd6df2844cfd7cffd2363c561337ac74d18a1fb5.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $\\angle CAD.$\n\nThe measure of $\\angle CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(\\angle BAE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle DAE).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx = 110^\\circ - 40^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 50^\\circ.\n$$",
